{"duration_api_ms": 44073, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "df7500bd-6aa1-4923-8ede-41ef8303b648", "total_cost_usd": 0.09770360000000002, "usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 23626, "cache_read_input_tokens": 289686, "output_tokens": 4277, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 894}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 23626, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1565, "cache_read_input_tokens": 35129, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 450, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 450}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 98, "outputTokens": 4277, "cacheReadInputTokens": 289686, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 23626, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.09770360000000002, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 894, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 23, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Now I have a complete picture. Let me summarize what an implementer of SPEC.md would need to know:\n\n## Summary: Three Systems, Two Unresolved Date Formats, and Five Commands\n\n**The three systems and their export formats:**\n\n| System | Date Format | Amount Format | Column Names | Special Handling |\n|--------|-------------|---------------|--------------|------------------|\n| **A (Ardent)** | ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` | Decimal dollars | `entry_id, posted_on, account, memo, amount, currency` | May have quoted fields; reader currently rejects them |\n| **B (Borough)** | ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` | **Integer cents** — divide by 100 | `sys, doc_no, value_date, acct, descr, amount, cur` | Repeats system letter in each row for safe concatenation |\n| **C (Calder)** | **DD/MM/YYYY** | Decimal dollars | `ref, txn_date, ledger_acct, narrative, gross_amount, ccy` | Banner and trailer; trailer row count is advisory only |\n\n**Building blocks already in place:**\n\n- `Record`: A frozen dataclass (record_id, source_system, date, account_code, account_name, description, amount). All amounts must be `Decimal` dollars, all dates must be `datetime.date`.\n- `RECORD_COLUMNS`: The fixed output header order for normalized files.\n- `Settings`: Holds `decimals`, `unknown_account_label`, `tolerance` (Decimal), `account_code_pattern`, and `source_path`.\n- `mapping.account_name(code, unknown_label)`: Returns the account name for a code, or the unknown label if the code is not in the map.\n- `cli.emit(line)`: The only place in the package that prints; everything the user reads goes through it.\n- Parsers return raw strings keyed by their system's own column names; the caller interprets them.\n\n**House rules binding any new code:**\n\n1. **Money is always `Decimal`** from read to print; never `float`. Borough amounts come in as cents and must be converted.\n2. **Rounding is half-to-even**: `Decimal.quantize()` uses it by default. Round once at display time, not individual postings.\n3. **Logging goes through `ledgerkit.log.get_logger(__name__)`**; warnings about data go to the logger, not stdout.\n4. **Every public function carries full type annotations** on parameters and return type.\n5. **No print in library code**; use `cli.emit()` in the CLI layer only.\n6. **Readers are shape-only** (header/trailer/quoting); interpretation belongs to the code that knows which system it is.\n7. **Never edit `config/`**, not even to add files. Settings override comes from `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` environment variable.\n8. **Standard library only**; no new dependencies.\n9. **Flag names are fixed**: `--out`, `--by`, `--records`, `--include-refunds`, `--tolerance`, `--config`.\n\n**The five features to implement:**\n\n1. **`ingest`**: Read any number of files from any mix of systems, produce one normalized CSV with all postings, ordered by (date, system, record_id), no filtering.\n2. **`report`**: Group normalized postings by account or month, total amounts, show with configured decimal places. Refunds are excluded by default unless `--include-refunds` is passed.\n3. **`reconcile`**: Find account-month combinations where two or more systems disagree by more than tolerance (Decimal comparison); report spread and per-system totals.\n4. **`validate`**: Reject rows that don't match field count, date format, amount format, or account code pattern; log warnings, exit 2 if any fail.\n5. **`--config PATH`**: Global option (before subcommand) that changes where settings come from, respecting the layering (built-in defaults → `config/settings.toml` → override file).\n\nAll five features must respect the existing `Record` and `Settings` types, parse dates correctly for each system (ISO for A and B, DD/MM/YYYY for C), and convert Borough amounts from cents to dollars.", "ttft_ms": 1355, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 45096, "uuid": "4438d5f6-2872-4803-9159-29960ff4644b", "ttft_stream_ms": 859, "time_to_request_ms": 133, "first_content_frame_ms": 1104, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 46.2, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
