{"duration_api_ms": 10864, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "df7500bd-6aa1-4923-8ede-41ef8303b648", "total_cost_usd": 0.0100429, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 241, "cache_read_input_tokens": 39609, "output_tokens": 1118, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 655}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 241, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1118, "cache_read_input_tokens": 39609, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 241, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 241}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 10, "outputTokens": 1118, "cacheReadInputTokens": 39609, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 241, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.0100429, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 655, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 1, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "**Amounts:**\n\n- **System A**: Already decimal dollars, two decimal places. Example: `239.55` → just parse as `Decimal(\"239.55\")`\n- **System B**: **Integer cents, not dollars.** Example: `25440` is $254.40, not $25,440. The `to_major_units()` function in `system_b.py` shows the rule: divide by 100 and quantize to 0.01. This is the gotcha — two importers have been caught treating it as dollars.\n- **System C**: Already decimal dollars, two decimal places. Example: `386.54` → just parse as `Decimal(\"386.54\")`\n\n**Result:** Amounts are only directly comparable after converting System B from cents to dollars.\n\n---\n\n**Dates:**\n\n- **System A**: ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`. Example: `2026-01-03` → parse with `datetime.date.fromisoformat()`\n- **System B**: ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`. Example: `2026-01-07` → parse with `datetime.date.fromisoformat()`\n- **System C**: **Day-first format `DD/MM/YYYY`, not `MM/DD/YYYY`.** Example: `02/01/2026` is January 2nd, not February 1st. The parser comment warns: read month-first and \"rows past the twelfth of a month blow up, while the rows on or before it quietly land in the wrong month.\"\n\n**Result:** Dates are only directly comparable after parsing System C's DD/MM/YYYY format correctly (not assuming MM/DD/YYYY).\n\n---\n\nSo before `ingest` normalizes anything, it needs to:\n1. Convert all Borough amounts by dividing by 100\n2. Parse all Calder dates as day-first, not month-first\n\nThe readers hand back raw strings; the conversion and parsing happens in whoever builds `Record` objects from those raw strings.", "ttft_ms": 7320, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 11116, "uuid": "60ac9812-2edc-46fa-ae77-e846432f00af", "ttft_stream_ms": 945, "time_to_request_ms": 284, "first_content_frame_ms": 1175, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 13.0, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors"