e by default in report totals (amendment to original SPEC)\n3. ❓ **Open question** (unverified): The `--include-refunds` flag status — should it be kept as a no-op (for backward compatibility with scripts), or removed entirely since refunds are now included by default?\n\nAll other implementation requirements from the conclusion align with SPEC.md and CONVENTIONS.md:\n- System conversions: Ardent (no conversion), Borough (cents→dollars), Calder (DD/MM/YYYY parsing)\n- Decimal amounts, half-to-even rounding, full type annotations\n- Use `cli.emit()` for output, `ledgerkit.log.get_logger()` for logging\n- Fixed flag names\n\n**Should I proceed with implementing based on the conclusion's amendments (semicolons, refunds included by default), or do you need to clarify the `--include-refunds` flag handling first?**", "ttft_ms": 1741, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 23893, "uuid": "b79361bb-3a2b-4f26-ab16-1ec644185d7d", "ttft_stream_ms": 809, "time_to_request_ms": 134, "first_content_frame_ms": 1063, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "merge", "_wall_s": 25.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
