l rows to normalized Records with proper type conversions\n- Outputs comma-separated CSV with proper quoting\n- Creates parent directories automatically\n- Default output: `out/records.csv`\n- Summary line reports row count\n\n### 2. **`validate`** — reject malformed rows\n- Validates each row without writing\n- Checks date format per system (ISO for A/B, DD/MM/YYYY for C)\n- Validates amount parsing (cents for B, decimals for A/C)\n- Checks account code against configured pattern\n- Reports all invalid rows with line numbers\n- Exit code 2 when any row is rejected\n\n### 3. **`report`** — totals by account or month\n- Reads normalized CSV file\n- Groups postings by account code or month\n- **Outputs semicolon-separated format** (per amendment)\n- **Includes refunds by default** (per amendment)\n- Formats amounts with configured decimal places\n- Uses half-to-even rounding\n\n### 4. **`reconcile`** — where systems disagree\n- Reads normalized CSV file\n- Groups by account/month/system and calculates totals\n- Reports mismatches where spread exceeds tolerance\n- Formats all amounts with exactly 2 decimal places (SPEC requirement)\n- Shows which systems have data and which show as `-`\n\n### 5. **`--config`** — settings for one run\n- Global option before subcommand name\n- Points to alternate TOML settings file\n- Sets `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` environment variable\n- Works with all subcommands\n\n### Key Implementation Details\n- **System A**: ISO dates, decimal dollars → no conversion needed\n- **System B**: ISO dates, integer cents → converts to decimal dollars\n- **System C**: DD/MM/YYYY dates, decimal dollars → parses day-first\n- All amounts stored as `Decimal` (never float)\n- Uses `fields.split_record()` to properly handle quoted fields in System A exports\n- Refunds always included in ingest and report operations\n- Report uses `;` separator (amendment), reconcile output always shows 2 decimals\n\nAll existing tests pass, and the implementation respects all conventions in `docs/CONVENTIONS.md`.", "ttft_ms": 4247, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 392487, "uuid": "4aaa81a3-469e-4038-bb55-97aa4e6cf406", "ttft_stream_ms": 801, "time_to_request_ms": 142, "first_content_frame_ms": 1088, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "phase2", "_wall_s": 398.6, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin", "--resume", "30d613a4-45cd-4361-9f61-49739031941f"]}
